:{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"in Bazel 0.4.1, packages are defined in BUILD.bazel as well as BUILD files. But it don't work if an external repository have BUILD.bazel.\r\n\r\n### Description of the problem:\r\n\r\nHere is the sample of using BUILD.bazel file.\r\nhttps://github.com/lizan/bazel-build-external-samples\r\n\r\nBuilding it with `bazel build //:all` in it works fine.\r\n\r\nCreate another directory, with WORKSPACE file as following:\r\n```\r\ngit_repository(\r\n    name = \"examples_cpp\",\r\n    remote = \"https://github.com/lizan/bazel-build-external-samples\",\r\n    commit = \"577d40436c6c15aec17a4a9801ded28001805a2f\",\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd do `bazel build @examples_cpp//:all` will result:\r\n```\r\nERROR: while parsing '@examples_cpp//:all': no such package '@examples_cpp//': BUILD file not found on package path.\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt works just fine if the samples is using BUILD instead of BUILD.bazel, but BUILD.bazel should work too.\r\n\r\n### Environment info\r\n* Operating System:\r\nMac OS X 10.11\r\n\r\n* Bazel version (output of `bazel info release`):\r\nBuild label: 0.4.1\r\nBuild target: bazel-out/local-fastbuild/bin/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/bazel/BazelServer_deploy.jar\r\nBuild time: Wed Nov 30 09:13:20 2016 (1480497200)\r\nBuild timestamp: 1480497200\r\nBuild timestamp as int: 1480497200","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/star